export anchor TradingTerminalStyle:
    number: 305
    screen: OpsMonitor
    name: Trading terminal
    idea: A dense black terminal of seven numbered panels with orange title bars, a service ticker tape, function key app tabs and all caps monospace readouts.
    base: dark
    palette:
        black: #000000, the page, gaps between panels and the style sheet
        panel: #0c0c0c, panel bodies
        rule: #3a3a3a, panel borders and dotted table rules
        ink: #f2e9da, body text and figures
        muted: #aaa092, labels and axes
        orange: #ff9a1f, panel title bars, the logo block, table headers, request bars and the primary button
        yellow: #ffd23f, times, the peak bar, Degraded, Investigating and p95
        green: #3ddc84, Healthy and Resolved
        cyan: #5cc8ff, Recovered and p50
        red: #ff6161, the error line and Firing
        focus: #ffffff, a white focus outline over an orange halo
    type:
        Monospace for everything, ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo, Consolas,
        Liberation Mono, at 12px and 1.4. Panel titles 12px bold black on
        orange in caps, quote figures 16px bold, the incident number 18px
        bold yellow. Status words and the alert wire are in caps.
    layout:
        A command bar runs across the top over a 2px orange rule. It holds
        an orange BRIGHTWORK OPS block, the apps as function keys F1
        PROJECTS to F5 OPS with F5 inverted cream, a CMD prompt field
        reading OPS PROD 24H and a PROD 24H readout. A ticker tape follows
        with each service in caps, its status shape and short word, uptime
        and metric, scrolling sideways inside itself on small screens. The
        wall is a 12 column grid with 2px black gaps. Panel 1 is the
        service board table, panel 2 the requests per minute chart as 24
        orange hourly bars with the 14.00 bar yellow and a HI and LO quote
        row, panel 3 the error rate line with base and spike quotes, panel
        4 latency as stepped p50 and p95 lines, panel 5 the incident with a
        yellow border, panel 6 the alert wire as headline rows and panel 7
        the deploy blotter table. A footer line repeats the description.
        Below 1000px panels pair up and at phone width they stack, with
        tables scrolling inside their panels.
    spacing: A 2px gap between panels, 6px panel padding, 4px by 6px table cells.
    density: Very dense. Seven panels and a ticker on one wide screen.
    corners: Square everywhere.
    borders: 1px #3a3a3a panels, dotted row rules, a yellow border on the incident panel, a 2px orange rule under the command bar.
    shadows: None.
    icons:
        12px status shapes before caps words, a ringed tick for HEALTHY, a
        triangle for DEGRADED, a circular arrow for RECOVERED, a bolt for
        FIRING, a tick for RESOLVED and a magnifier for INVESTIGATING.
    focus: A 2px white outline with a 4px orange halo.
    tone: Terse terminal caps, such as HI, SPIKE, ALERT WIRE, DEPLOY BLOTTER and 3 FILLS.
